WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.353
Let us finish Module 6 by reviewing

00:00:02.379 --> 00:00:05.408
the main ideas A module is usually

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:08.197
one Python file that contains reusable code

00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:11.697
Python provides many built-in modules and we

00:00:11.724 --> 00:00:14.566
can also create our own modules An

00:00:14.592 --> 00:00:16.789
import statement gives a program access to

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.908
code from another module We can import

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:22.250
a complete module use an alias or

00:00:22.276 --> 00:00:25.763
selectively import a specific tool A package

00:00:25.789 --> 00:00:28.000
is a folder that groups related modules

00:00:28.026 --> 00:00:31.539
together Packages become useful as a project

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:35.039
grows and contains several related files A

00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:37.461
class is a blueprint for creating objects

00:00:38.382 --> 00:00:40.658
The class describes the attributes an object

00:00:40.684 --> 00:00:42.605
stores and the methods it can perform

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:45.605
An object is one actual instance of

00:00:45.618 --> 00:00:48.658
a class One class can create many

00:00:48.671 --> 00:00:50.829
objects and each object can store its

00:00:50.842 --> 00:00:54.434
own values Attributes are data stored inside

00:00:54.461 --> 00:00:57.803
an object Methods are functions that belong

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:00.684
to a class The word self refers

00:01:00.711 --> 00:01:02.316
to the current object and allows a

00:01:02.342 --> 00:01:04.711
method to use that object's own attributes

00:01:05.632 --> 00:01:07.237
Remember that you do not need to

00:01:07.263 --> 00:01:11.118
use classes everywhere Use the simplest structure

00:01:11.145 --> 00:01:14.355
that clearly fits the task For additional

00:01:14.382 --> 00:01:17.474
practice try creating a class named StudentScore

00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:19.855
Give it a student name and a

00:01:19.868 --> 00:01:22.921
list of scores Then create a method

00:01:22.947 --> 00:01:26.461
that calculates the average score After that

00:01:26.671 --> 00:01:29.447
create two StudentScore objects with different
values

00:01:29.461 --> 00:01:31.316
and print the average for each object

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.079
If you can explain the difference between

00:01:34.105 --> 00:01:36.408
a module a package a class and

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:37.908
an object and if you can read

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:40.079
the class examples in this module then

00:01:40.092 --> 00:01:42.474
you have reached the main goal The

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:46.632
larger lesson is organization As analytics projects

00:01:46.645 --> 00:01:48.803
grow good structure makes code easier to

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:51.579
reuse easier to test easier to explain

00:01:51.789 --> 00:01:54.539
and easier to maintain In the next

00:01:54.566 --> 00:01:57.079
module we will continue building our Python

00:01:57.105 --> 00:01:59.553
skills with more advanced programming techniques
